  },
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "What software quality means once your application has **100+ developers**.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "<div class=\"pt-12\">↵ <span class=\"px-2 py-1 rounded cursor-pointer\" hover=\"bg-white bg-opacity-10\">↵ Press <kbd>space</kbd> for next slide↵ </span>↵</div>",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "---↵layout: default↵---",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "**At 20–50 developers**, quality means \"does the code work?\"<br>↵**At 100+ developers**, quality means",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "\"Does the system let 100 people change it on Monday without breaking the customers' Tuesday?\"",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The defect is not in the code.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "**The defect is in the seam.**",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "---↵layout: two-cols↵layoutClass: gap-8↵---",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The system reflects the org chart.<br><br>↵A team changes the contract on Monday.<br>↵Three teams over read the old contract on Tuesday.<br><br>↵**The seam breaks.**",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "::right::",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding headcount stops adding velocity at ~50 devs.<br><br>↵Every new dev inherits a bigger mental model.<br>↵The marginal cost of context-switching dominates.<br><br>↵**Adding people slows you down.**",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "---↵layout: two-cols↵layoutClass: gap-8↵---",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "100 teams, 100 definitions of \"done\".<br><br>↵Each team's local quality is fine.<br>↵The aggregate quality is unknowable.<br><br>↵**No one owns the seam.**",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "::right::",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The team rewarded is the team that ships.<br><br>↵The team penalised is the team whose contract changed underneath them.<br><br>↵**Doing the right thing costs you; doing the wrong thing pays.**",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "---",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "| What to measure | What to change | What to stop measuring |↵|---|---|---|↵| Delivery lead time | Conway drift | Lines of code |↵| Deploy frequency | Cognitive load | PR count |↵| MTTR | Federated quality | Coverage % |↵| Change fail rate | Incentive inversion | Individual velocity |",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "And the **one question**:",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "\"If we changed this seam on Monday, which team would notice on Tuesday — and how long would it take them to find out?\"",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "slides",
        "title": "The Quality Ceiling — Slides",
        "url": "/blog/slides/"
      }
    },
